export default {"id":"djing-level-4","number":4,"title":"Windows Configuration and Cue Path · Gate B","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"Live performance fails when the operating system interrupts the audio buffer. Foundations of Digital DJing frames three pillars: OS optimization, Live architecture, and controller integration. Without OS stability, later skill work is confo","modules":[{"id":"djing-m-4-1","code":"4","title":"Windows Configuration and Cue Path · Gate B","blurb":"Live performance fails when the operating system interrupts the audio buffer. Foundations of Digital DJing frames three pillars: OS optimization, Live architecture, and controller integration. Without OS stability, later skill work is confo","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"djing-l-o-4","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Module 4 — Windows Configuration and Cue Path · Gate B","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Objective:</strong> Configure the computer as a stable real-time instrument; verify Main ≠ Cue by listening.   <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Intermediate systems laboratory — configuration and verification.   <strong>Sources:</strong> <em>Foundations of Digital DJing</em> (Windows real-time audio); <em>How-to-DJ</em> Module 7 Banana and §5.3 cue; Ableton Live 12 Manual §18.6 Soloing and Cueing; ASIO practice for Windows DJ hosts."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"djing-l-4-1-1","title":"4.1.1 — Windows 11 as a Real-Time Audio Host","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Rationale","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Live performance fails when the operating system interrupts the audio buffer. <em>Foundations of Digital DJing</em> frames three pillars: OS optimization, Live architecture, and controller integration. Without OS stability, later skill work is confounded by underruns and connection failures."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Windows checklist (performance-oriented)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Apply as a workstation profile for practice and performance machines. Details vary by hardware; verify each change."},{"type":"table","headers":["Area","Direction","Rationale"],"rows":[["Power plan","High performance or audio workstation; avoid aggressive CPU parking","Reduced C-state thrashing that causes buffer underruns"],["Min/max processor state","Often locked high on show machines","Avoids downclock stalls on transients"],["USB selective suspend","Disabled","Controllers and interfaces must not sleep mid-set"],["USB hubs “allow computer to turn off”","Unchecked where present","Same failure class"],["Background startup applications","Reduced","Network and background activity can cause DPC spikes"],["Audio path","ASIO into Live (vendor ASIO preferred when available)","Avoids Windows shared-mode latency path"],["Sample rate","Unified across devices in the chain","Rate mismatch produces glitches and pitch errors"],["Buffer","Start stable (often 512 samples for heavy full-track Complex/Pro loads; lower only if CPU allows)","Very small buffers favor light tracking; multi full-song warp often needs larger buffers"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"<em>Foundations</em> notes that DJ loads (full-track stretch, multiple layers) often favor larger buffers (for example 512–1024) for multi-hour stability over minimal latency figures."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Long playback test (required)","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Load a representative Set (two full Complex/Pro tracks, EQ, light return effects).  ","Play 45–60 minutes continuously while launching clips occasionally.  ","Log clicks, dropouts, MIDI freezes, thermal throttling, and USB resets.  ","Correct root causes before treating remaining issues as DJing skill problems."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Common errors","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Attributing OS or DPC problems to Live alone  ","Forcing 64-sample buffers with multiple Complex Pro full tracks  ","Mixing sample rates among Banana, interface, and Live  ","Treating a few minutes of stability as proof of show readiness  "],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"Laboratory 4.1.1","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Complete the checklist on the machine in use; run the long test; produce a half-page stability report (changes made, buffer and sample rate, failures observed, residual risks)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Pass criteria:</strong> 45 minutes or more clean, or residual issues documented with mitigation. ASIO path confirmed in Live audio preferences."}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"djing-l-4-2-1","title":"4.2.1 — Main versus Cue (Banana First) · Gate B","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"4.2.1 — Main versus Cue (Banana First) · Gate B","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Manual requirements (Ableton)","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"From Live 12 Manual <em>Mixing</em> §18.6:"},{"type":"list","items":["Cueing requires an interface path with at least two stereo outputs (four mono outputs), or a virtual multi-out that presents multiple pairs to Live.  ","Set Main Out and Cue Out to different pairs.  ","Set Solo/Cue mode to Cue (not classic Solo that mutes the mix for monitoring).  ","Track Cue switches send that track to Cue Out; Track Activator still controls presence on Main.  ","Cue Volume controls cue loudness; browser preview also routes to Cue Out when cueing is active."],"ordered":false},{"type":"heading","text":"Banana-first configuration (academy policy)","level":3},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Primary path:</strong> Voicemeeter Banana provides multi-out → Live ASIO → map Main and Cue to distinct Banana outputs → speakers on Main path, headphones on Cue path.   <strong>Alternate:</strong> Hardware multi-out interface (Main 1/2, Cue 3/4)."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Scope note:</strong> Exact Banana channel indices are practical configurations. No single official Ableton and Banana channel map is treated as authoritative. Verify by listening on every cold start."},{"type":"heading","text":"Verification procedure (Gate B core)","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Track A playing to Main only — room or speakers hear A; headphones silent if cue is off.  ","Cue B — headphones hear B (and/or cue blend according to monitoring habit); speakers must not present full-level B if B’s Track Activator is off or B is not in the main mix.  ","Deliberately set Main and Cue to the same output once to learn the failure condition.  ","Restore correct routing; re-verify; write a personal channel map card."],"ordered":true},{"type":"heading","text":"Common errors","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Main equal to Cue (audience hears cue monitoring)  ","Solo mode instead of Cue mode  ","Headphone amplifier on the wrong Banana bus  ","Assuming correct routing without the listening verification  "],"ordered":false},{"type":"heading","text":"Gate B — self-assessment","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Long playback test logged  ","[ ] Main Out ≠ Cue Out in Live  ","[ ] Solo/Cue = Cue  ","[ ] Listening verification passed on a cold start  ","[ ] Personal Banana or interface map card exists  "],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>If criteria are not met:</strong> do not proceed to Session template building as if cue routing were optional. Correct routing first."}]},{"type":"step","title":"Module 4 checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["[ ] Windows ASIO path stable under DJ-like load  ","[ ] Gate B Main ≠ Cue proven by listening  ","[ ] Channel map card saved with the DJ template (Module 5)  "],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
